<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Detailed Codec Formalisms</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Predictive Masking: Rate-Accurate Formulation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:N}</annotation></semantics></math> be the token sequence. Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}\subset\{1,\dots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}\subset\{1,\dots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the masked indices, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{M}|=\lfloor p_{\text{mask}}N\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>mask</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{M}|=\lfloor p_{\text{mask}}N\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\{1,\dots,N\}\setminus\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\{1,\dots,N\}\setminus\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> the kept indices with fraction <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{keep}}=1-p_{\text{mask}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>keep</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>mask</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{keep}}=1-p_{\text{mask}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote model surprisal at <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}=-\log_{2}q_{\theta}(x_{i}\mid X_{\setminus i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}=-\log_{2}q_{\theta}(x_{i}\mid X_{\setminus i})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Mask set selection.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We use windowed equalisation. Partition <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\dots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\dots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math> into windows <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{w}\}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{w}\}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>; choose per-window thresholds <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A1.E2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E2X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bigcup_{w}\bigl\{i\in W_{w}:s_{i}\leq\tau_{w}\bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mi>w</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bigcup_{w}\bigl\{i\in W_{w}:s_{i}\leq\tau_{w}\bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E2Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\mathcal{M}\cap W_{w}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\mathcal{M}\cap W_{w}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\big\lfloor p_{\text{mask}}\cdot|W_{w}|\big\rfloor." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>mask</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big\lfloor p_{\text{mask}}\cdot|W_{w}|\big\rfloor.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We cap masked runs by enforcing a maximum run-length, which bounds local error cascades.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Payload.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Positions are encoded with a succinct bitvector; the cost satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{bits}_{\text{pos}}^{\text{PM}}\;\approx\;N\min\bigl\{H_{2}(p_{\text{keep}}),\ \mathcal{R}_{\text{RLE}}(p_{\text{keep}})\bigr\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext>bits</mtext><mtext>pos</mtext><mtext>PM</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>keep</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>RLE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>keep</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{bits}_{\text{pos}}^{\text{PM}}\;\approx\;N\min\bigl\{H_{2}(p_{\text{keep}}),\ \mathcal{R}_{\text{RLE}}(p_{\text{keep}})\bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the binary entropy and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\text{RLE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>RLE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\text{RLE}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the expected rate for run-length encoding. Kept tokens are entropy-coded in natural order with an auxiliary autoregressive coder <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{bits}_{\text{tok}}^{\text{PM}}\;=\;\sum_{i\in\mathcal{S}}-\log_{2}P_{\psi}\big(x_{i}\mid x_{j}:j\in\mathcal{S},j&lt;i\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mtext>bits</mtext><mtext>tok</mtext><mtext>PM</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{bits}_{\text{tok}}^{\text{PM}}\;=\;\sum_{i\in\mathcal{S}}-\log_{2}P_{\psi}\big(x_{i}\mid x_{j}:j\in\mathcal{S},j&lt;i\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Total payload bits for PM are <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{bits}_{\text{PM}}=\text{bits}_{\text{pos}}^{\text{PM}}+\text{bits}_{\text{tok}}^{\text{PM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>bits</mtext><mtext>PM</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>bits</mtext><mtext>pos</mtext><mtext>PM</mtext></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mtext>bits</mtext><mtext>tok</mtext><mtext>PM</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{bits}_{\text{PM}}=\text{bits}_{\text{pos}}^{\text{PM}}+\text{bits}_{\text{tok}}^{\text{PM}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reconstruction.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We deterministically infill <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{i}\}_{i\in\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{i}\}_{i\in\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\max" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\max</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid X_{\setminus\mathcal{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid X_{\setminus\mathcal{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>, using the same specialisation from <a href="#S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" title="Stage 1: Model Specialisation. ‣ 3.1 Compression Pipeline ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ The Lossy Horizon: Error-Bounded Predictive Coding for Lossy Text Compression (Episode I)" class="ltx_ref">Stage 1</a>. The run-length cap guarantees at least one ground-truth token per window, which stabilises the local context during decoding.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Error-Bounded Predictive Coding: Rank-Indexed Residuals</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> be selected as above. For each <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{i}(\cdot)=q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid X_{\setminus\mathcal{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}(\cdot)=q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid X_{\setminus\mathcal{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> be the MLM distribution and let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}\in\{1,2,\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}\in\{1,2,\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the rank of the ground-truth token <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in the descending order of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s probabilities. Fix a rank threshold <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Payload.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Positions are coded as in (<a href="#A1.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ Payload. ‣ A.1 Predictive Masking: Rate-Accurate Formulation ‣ Appendix A Detailed Codec Formalisms ‣ The Lossy Horizon: Error-Bounded Predictive Coding for Lossy Text Compression (Episode I)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). We introduce an override flag <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="z_{i}=\mathbf{1}[r_{i}&gt;1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}=\mathbf{1}[r_{i}&gt;1]</annotation></semantics></math> and encode it with a Bernoulli coder. With masked-set top-1 accuracy <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}=\Pr(r_{i}=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}=\Pr(r_{i}=1)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{bits}_{\text{flag}}^{\text{EPC}}\;\approx\;|\mathcal{M}|H_{2}(1-p_{1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext>bits</mtext><mtext>flag</mtext><mtext>EPC</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{bits}_{\text{flag}}^{\text{EPC}}\;\approx\;|\mathcal{M}|H_{2}(1-p_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq r_{i}\leq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq r_{i}\leq K</annotation></semantics></math>, we transmit a rank index with code length <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\text{rank}}(r_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>rank</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\text{rank}}(r_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}&gt;K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}&gt;K</annotation></semantics></math>, we fall back to the full token code of length <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. The correction stream cost is</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{bits}_{\text{corr}}^{\text{EPC}}=\sum_{i\in\mathcal{M}}\bigl(\mathbf{1}[2\leq r_{i}\leq K]\cdot c_{\text{rank}}(r_{i})+\mathbf{1}[r_{i}&gt;K]\cdot\ell(x_{i})\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mtext>bits</mtext><mtext>corr</mtext><mtext>EPC</mtext></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>rank</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{bits}_{\text{corr}}^{\text{EPC}}=\sum_{i\in\mathcal{M}}\bigl(\mathbf{1}[2\leq r_{i}\leq K]\cdot c_{\text{rank}}(r_{i})+\mathbf{1}[r_{i}&gt;K]\cdot\ell(x_{i})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Total payload bits for EPC are <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{bits}_{\text{EPC}}\approx\text{bits}_{\text{pos}}^{\text{PM}}+\text{bits}_{\text{flag}}^{\text{EPC}}+\text{bits}_{\text{corr}}^{\text{EPC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>bits</mtext><mtext>EPC</mtext></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>bits</mtext><mtext>pos</mtext><mtext>PM</mtext></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mtext>bits</mtext><mtext>flag</mtext><mtext>EPC</mtext></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mtext>bits</mtext><mtext>corr</mtext><mtext>EPC</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{bits}_{\text{EPC}}\approx\text{bits}_{\text{pos}}^{\text{PM}}+\text{bits}_{\text{flag}}^{\text{EPC}}+\text{bits}_{\text{corr}}^{\text{EPC}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Distortion control.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If fallback is enabled for all <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}&gt;K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}&gt;K</annotation></semantics></math>, EPC reconstructs the masked subset losslessly. In the lossy regime, we can disable the fallback or constrain it with a budget <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The masked-set token error rate <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{masked}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>masked</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{masked}}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-increasing in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. This exposes two orthogonal controls: <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{mask}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>mask</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{mask}}</annotation></semantics></math> trades positions versus modelling load, while <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> interpolate between a cheap residual stream and exact correction.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reconstruction.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At decode, we run the same specialised MLM to obtain the ranked list at each <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, apply rank overrides where provided, and otherwise use <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\max" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\max</annotation></semantics></math> as in PM.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Vector Quantisation: Stabilised, Bounded-Error Formulation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The goal is to train exactly what we deploy: keys/values are quantised during training, scheduled self-feeding removes train-test mismatch, and codebooks are learnt via EMA with utilisation regularisation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> be input tokens. The transformer has <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> heads. At layer <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, token <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> has hidden state <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}^{(\ell)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}^{(\ell)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. For head <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, queries, keys, and values are computed as <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}^{(\ell,h)}=h_{t}^{(\ell-1)}W_{Q}^{\ell,h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}^{(\ell,h)}=h_{t}^{(\ell-1)}W_{Q}^{\ell,h}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{u}^{(\ell,h)}=h_{u}^{(\ell-1)}W_{K}^{\ell,h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{u}^{(\ell,h)}=h_{u}^{(\ell-1)}W_{K}^{\ell,h}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{u}^{(\ell,h)}=h_{u}^{(\ell-1)}W_{V}^{\ell,h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{u}^{(\ell,h)}=h_{u}^{(\ell-1)}W_{V}^{\ell,h}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\cdot}^{\ell,h}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\cdot}^{\ell,h}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each head maintains two codebooks <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{K}^{\ell,h}=\{c_{K,j}^{\ell,h}\}_{j=1}^{K_{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{K}^{\ell,h}=\{c_{K,j}^{\ell,h}\}_{j=1}^{K_{K}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{V}^{\ell,h}=\{c_{V,j}^{\ell,h}\}_{j=1}^{K_{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{V}^{\ell,h}=\{c_{V,j}^{\ell,h}\}_{j=1}^{K_{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\cdot,j}^{\ell,h}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\cdot,j}^{\ell,h}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Quantise K/V at training time.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Nearest-neighbour quantisation maps vectors to codebook entries:</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{u}^{(\ell,h)}=\arg\min_{j}\|K_{u}^{(\ell,h)}-c_{K,j}^{\ell,h}\|_{2}^{2},\quad\tilde{K}_{u}^{(\ell,h)}=c_{K,\kappa_{u}^{(\ell,h)}}^{\ell,h}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>j</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{u}^{(\ell,h)}=\arg\min_{j}\|K_{u}^{(\ell,h)}-c_{K,j}^{\ell,h}\|_{2}^{2},\quad\tilde{K}_{u}^{(\ell,h)}=c_{K,\kappa_{u}^{(\ell,h)}}^{\ell,h},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and similarly for values <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> to get <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}_{u}^{(\ell,h)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}_{u}^{(\ell,h)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Attention then uses these quantised vectors:</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E8X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{t,u}^{(\ell,h)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{t,u}^{(\ell,h)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{softmax}_{u}\left(\frac{Q_{t}^{(\ell,h)}\,\tilde{K}_{u}^{(\ell,h)\top}}{\sqrt{d_{h}}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{softmax}_{u}\left(\frac{Q_{t}^{(\ell,h)}\,\tilde{K}_{u}^{(\ell,h)\top}}{\sqrt{d_{h}}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E8Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle o_{t}^{(\ell,h)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle o_{t}^{(\ell,h)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{u=1}^{T}A_{t,u}^{(\ell,h)}\tilde{V}_{u}^{(\ell,h)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{u=1}^{T}A_{t,u}^{(\ell,h)}\tilde{V}_{u}^{(\ell,h)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We apply the straight-through estimator (STE) for backpropagation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Scheduled self-feeding.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To remove exposure bias between training and testing, we replace teacher activations with their quantised counterparts with probability <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> at the training step <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, using an inverse sigmoid schedule. At test time, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\tau}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\tau}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">EMA codebooks and commitment.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Codebooks are updated using an exponential moving average (EMA) with decay <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>. We also added a commitment loss:</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{commit}}=\beta\sum_{u}\|\mathrm{sg}[K_{u}]-\tilde{K}_{u}\|_{2}^{2}+\gamma\sum_{u}\|K_{u}-\mathrm{sg}[\tilde{K}_{u}]\|_{2}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>commit</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>u</mi></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>u</mi></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{commit}}=\beta\sum_{u}\|\mathrm{sg}[K_{u}]-\tilde{K}_{u}\|_{2}^{2}+\gamma\sum_{u}\|K_{u}-\mathrm{sg}[\tilde{K}_{u}]\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and analogously for <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{sg}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{sg}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> is the stop-gradient operator.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Code usage regularisation.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To avoid dead codes, we penalise the divergence of the empirical code usage distribution from a uniform prior.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Full training objective.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The final loss combines the standard cross-entropy language modelling loss with VQ-specific terms:</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}+\mathcal{L}_{\text{commit}}+\mathcal{L}_{\text{util}}^{K}+\mathcal{L}_{\text{util}}^{V}+\mathcal{L}_{\text{sem}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>commit</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>util</mtext><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>util</mtext><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>sem</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}+\mathcal{L}_{\text{commit}}+\mathcal{L}_{\text{util}}^{K}+\mathcal{L}_{\text{util}}^{V}+\mathcal{L}_{\text{sem}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{sem}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>sem</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{sem}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a lightweight semantic consistency loss. Training uses the quantised <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{K},\tilde{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{K},\tilde{V}</annotation></semantics></math> (blended by <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>), EMA updates, and the STE.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section><div class="ltx_rdf" about="" property="dcterms:title" content="The Lossy Horizon: Error-Bounded Predictive Coding for Lossy Text Compression (Episode I)"></div>

</article>
</div>
</div>
